{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"language-registration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language Registration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language registration is the main bundle-size control in TanStack Highlight."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-selective-highlighter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a selective highlighter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The resulting registry contains three definitions plus their aliases. It does not load a global grammar catalog."}]},{"type":"code","value":"highlighter.listLanguages()\n// ['json', 'shell', 'tsx']\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('bash')\n// 'shell'\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('python')\n// 'plaintext'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aliases belong to definitions. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bash"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves only because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shell"},{"type":"text","value":" was registered."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fallback-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fallback behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default fallback name is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plaintext"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const result = highlighter.highlight('<unsafe>', {\n  lang: 'not-registered',\n})\n\nresult.lang\n// 'plaintext'\n\nresult.html\n// The angle brackets are escaped.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can choose another registered fallback language:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  fallbackLanguage: 'json',\n  languages: [json],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unknown inputs will then be tokenized as JSON. An unregistered fallback name still produces escaped plaintext under that name, but registering "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plaintext"},{"type":"text","value":" is clearer when plain output is intentional."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"root-convenience-entry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Root convenience entry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package root constructs a highlighter with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allLanguages"},{"type":"text","value":" and exports bound helpers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  defaultHighlighter,\n  highlight,\n  highlightToHtml,\n  listLanguages,\n  normalizeLanguage,\n  renderCodeBlockData,\n  tokenize,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is convenient, but importing any bound helper retains the all-language registry. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/highlight/core"},{"type":"text","value":" when browser size matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core helpers re-exported from the root, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHighlighter"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineLanguage"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"escapeHtml"},{"type":"text","value":", don't need that registry. Importing only those helpers lets a compatible bundler remove every built-in language."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"share-one-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Share one registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the highlighter once at module scope:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// code-highlighter.ts\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is no benefit to creating one per block. The registry is immutable after construction and safe to reuse across server requests and client renders."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"aggregate-imports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregate imports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The aggregate entry exposes every shipped language module:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { json, shell, tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tree-shaking bundler can remove unused definitions because the package is side-effect free. Prefer direct subpaths when the bundle must make isolation explicit:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../language-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language Support"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for every name and alias."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"language-registration","text":"Language Registration","level":1},{"id":"create-a-selective-highlighter","text":"Create a selective highlighter","level":2},{"id":"fallback-behavior","text":"Fallback behavior","level":2},{"id":"root-convenience-entry","text":"Root convenience entry","level":2},{"id":"share-one-registry","text":"Share one registry","level":2},{"id":"aggregate-imports","text":"Aggregate imports","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Language Registration\n\nLanguage registration is the main bundle-size control in TanStack Highlight.\n\n## Create a selective highlighter\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nThe resulting registry contains three definitions plus their aliases. It does not load a global grammar catalog.\n\n```ts\nhighlighter.listLanguages()\n// ['json', 'shell', 'tsx']\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('bash')\n// 'shell'\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('python')\n// 'plaintext'\n```\n\nAliases belong to definitions. `bash` resolves only because `shell` was registered.\n\n## Fallback behavior\n\nThe default fallback name is `plaintext`:\n\n```ts\nconst result = highlighter.highlight('<unsafe>', {\n  lang: 'not-registered',\n})\n\nresult.lang\n// 'plaintext'\n\nresult.html\n// The angle brackets are escaped.\n```\n\nYou can choose another registered fallback language:\n\n```ts\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  fallbackLanguage: 'json',\n  languages: [json],\n})\n```\n\nUnknown inputs will then be tokenized as JSON. An unregistered fallback name still produces escaped plaintext under that name, but registering `plaintext` is clearer when plain output is intentional.\n\n## Root convenience entry\n\nThe package root constructs a highlighter with `allLanguages` and exports bound helpers:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  defaultHighlighter,\n  highlight,\n  highlightToHtml,\n  listLanguages,\n  normalizeLanguage,\n  renderCodeBlockData,\n  tokenize,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight'\n```\n\nThis is convenient, but importing any bound helper retains the all-language registry. Use `@tanstack/highlight/core` when browser size matters.\n\nCore helpers re-exported from the root, such as `createHighlighter`, `defineLanguage`, and `escapeHtml`, don't need that registry. Importing only those helpers lets a compatible bundler remove every built-in language.\n\n## Share one registry\n\nCreate the highlighter once at module scope:\n\n```ts\n// code-highlighter.ts\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nThere is no benefit to creating one per block. The registry is immutable after construction and safe to reuse across server requests and client renders.\n\n## Aggregate imports\n\nThe aggregate entry exposes every shipped language module:\n\n```ts\nimport { json, shell, tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages'\n```\n\nA tree-shaking bundler can remove unused definitions because the package is side-effect free. Prefer direct subpaths when the bundle must make isolation explicit:\n\n```ts\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\n```\n\nSee [Language Support](../language-support) for every name and alias.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Language Registration\n---\n\n# Language Registration\n\nLanguage registration is the main bundle-size control in TanStack Highlight.\n\n## Create a selective highlighter\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\nimport { shell } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/shell'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\n\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nThe resulting registry contains three definitions plus their aliases. It does not load a global grammar catalog.\n\n```ts\nhighlighter.listLanguages()\n// ['json', 'shell', 'tsx']\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('bash')\n// 'shell'\n\nhighlighter.normalizeLanguage('python')\n// 'plaintext'\n```\n\nAliases belong to definitions. `bash` resolves only because `shell` was registered.\n\n## Fallback behavior\n\nThe default fallback name is `plaintext`:\n\n```ts\nconst result = highlighter.highlight('<unsafe>', {\n  lang: 'not-registered',\n})\n\nresult.lang\n// 'plaintext'\n\nresult.html\n// The angle brackets are escaped.\n```\n\nYou can choose another registered fallback language:\n\n```ts\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  fallbackLanguage: 'json',\n  languages: [json],\n})\n```\n\nUnknown inputs will then be tokenized as JSON. An unregistered fallback name still produces escaped plaintext under that name, but registering `plaintext` is clearer when plain output is intentional.\n\n## Root convenience entry\n\nThe package root constructs a highlighter with `allLanguages` and exports bound helpers:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  defaultHighlighter,\n  highlight,\n  highlightToHtml,\n  listLanguages,\n  normalizeLanguage,\n  renderCodeBlockData,\n  tokenize,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight'\n```\n\nThis is convenient, but importing any bound helper retains the all-language registry. Use `@tanstack/highlight/core` when browser size matters.\n\nCore helpers re-exported from the root, such as `createHighlighter`, `defineLanguage`, and `escapeHtml`, don't need that registry. Importing only those helpers lets a compatible bundler remove every built-in language.\n\n## Share one registry\n\nCreate the highlighter once at module scope:\n\n```ts\n// code-highlighter.ts\nexport const highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [json, shell, tsx],\n})\n```\n\nThere is no benefit to creating one per block. The registry is immutable after construction and safe to reuse across server requests and client renders.\n\n## Aggregate imports\n\nThe aggregate entry exposes every shipped language module:\n\n```ts\nimport { json, shell, tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages'\n```\n\nA tree-shaking bundler can remove unused definitions because the package is side-effect free. Prefer direct subpaths when the bundle must make isolation explicit:\n\n```ts\nimport { json } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/json'\n```\n\nSee [Language Support](../language-support) for every name and alias.\n"}
